      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Several win chances. MAGIC ANDERSON (4) is a former NSW galloper who has won two of three for the new yard and both wins were at this trip. Hard to knock and expected to go close again. IMMINENT BOOM (6) finished second two runs back at Ilfracombe then improved last time out to score by 0.9 lengths over 1000m at Aramac. Has good speed and will take catching off the low draw. BESTOV (7) got off the mark over 1450m at Cairns last start, scoring by a nose. This is tougher but has upside and capable of another big run. KIJIVU (2) turned in a much better effort last time out to score by a nose over 1400m at Louth. Solid top-three prospects. ANDERS KISS (9) has ability and can do much better.",
